Chapter: ArithNarrowProven

 Checker-prover arithmetic arms of the bounded-signatures campaign:
 interval arithmetic over proven operand ranges proves a
 constant-plus-scaled-index store, the shape of the emit-time address
 tables. table-base + i * 8 with i a bounded parameter 0..65535 lands
 in 28968..553248, inside 0..4294967295 (CDX2053); the subtraction arm
 proves 70000 - i and the division arm proves a literal split by the
 shifted index. __heap-save proves as a structural heap-address fact.
 The unproven twin of each shape lives in errors/narrowing-unproven,
 rejected since CDX2051 became an error. The sidecars pin the proven
 diagnostics and the runtime values.

Section: Definitions

  Slot = record {
   addr : Integer between 0 and 4294967295,
   gap : Integer between 0 and 4294967295,
   eighth : Integer between 0 and 4294967295
  }

  Mark = record {
   at : Integer between 0 and 4294967295
  }

  table-base : Integer = 28968

  slot-at : Integer between 0 and 65535 -> Slot
  slot-at (i) = Slot {
   addr = table-base + i * 8,
   gap = 70000 - i,
   eighth = 65532 / (i + 1)
  }

  take-mark : Mark
  take-mark =
   let h = __heap-save
   in Mark { at = h }

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((slot-at 3).addr))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((slot-at 3).gap))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((slot-at 3).eighth))
   print-line-uni (if (take-mark).at > 0 then "mark-ok" else "mark-zero")
  end
